ation and disruption, a changed boot identity, and complete post-restart service recovery; fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot change.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe checks systemd and is unsupported on this OpenRC-based Alpine node, so it does not independently inventory failed OpenRC services.","The restart acknowledgement is a locally emitted scheduling marker rather than a provider-generated acknowledgement, although the ensuing connection loss, changed boot ID, fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service directly demonstrate that the reboot occurred."]}
